  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\n**The 1.3.x “observation/change‑feed cursor” behaviour applies** — the opaque, filter‑independent, durable position on Ordarium’s state‑change (commit‑observation) feed, with **fail‑closed cursor invalidation** (`InvalidCursorError`) and a capability guard (`LEDGER_CAPABILITY_REQUIRED`).\\n\\nThe behaviour described in `docs/release-commentary-1.2.0.md` — *“no notion of a change‑feed cursor and no cursor‑invalidation failure”* — does **not** apply to this integration.\\n\\n## Why (manifest beats commentary)\\n\\n| Layer | Artifact | Says |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Manifest (effective)** | `package.json:32-37`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml:15-18` | All four `@ordarium/*` deps pin `ordarium-v1.3.1` |\\n| **Resolved runtime** | `node_modules/@ordarium/{core,host-kit,ledger-sqlite}/package.json` | `\\\"version\\\": \\\"1.3.1\\\"` |\\n| **Capability surface** | `ledger-sqlite/dist/src/index.js:25`, `index.d.ts:37` | `stateChangeFeed: true` |\\n| **Contract** | `core/dist/src/types.d.ts` (`StateChangeFeed`, `StateChangePage`), `state.d.ts:28-32`, `errors.d.ts:95-101` | Feed exists; cursor always present; `InvalidCursorError` fails closed |\\n| **Commentary (self‑scoped)** | `docs/release-commentary",
